WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions for nightbell-promo.mp4 (40.0 s).

The text is the narration verbatim, from promo-video/scripts/narration.mjs.
Cue starts are the `at` frames in that file divided by 30; cue ends are the
start plus the measured duration of the corresponding take under
promo-video/audio/vo/. Two of the seven lines are split across two cues so no
cue holds more than about two lines of text on screen.

Re-check these against `npm run voiceover` in promo-video/ after any change to
the script or the scene budgets. The lines are anchored to cuts, so a re-budget
moves them.

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.215
Most uptime alerts are one more
notification you swipe away.

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.670
Nightbell runs entirely on your Android phone.

3
00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.948
No server, no account, no third party.

4
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.860
Four steps to add a monitor.

5
00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.519
Point it at anything that answers over HTTP.

6
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.120
Every check runs on the phone.

7
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.480
Your tokens never touch a third party.

8
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.676
When a check fails, Nightbell doesn't send you
something you can miss.

9
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.365
It takes the whole screen, and the alarm
loops until you acknowledge it.

10
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.920
Nightbell. The uptime monitor that needs
no server, no account,

11
00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.823
and actually wakes you up.
